---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
---

<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <title>How to Apply – Q-LUMEN</title>

        <style>
            :root {
                --qlumen-purple: #bd7de8ff;
                --qlumen-orange: #ff9b3dff;
                --qlumen-purple-soft: #efe1f9ff;
                --qlumen-orange-soft: #ffd9bbff;
            }

            .qlumen-gradient {
                background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--qlumen-purple), var(--qlumen-orange));
            }

            .qlumen-soft-gradient {
                background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--qlumen-purple-soft), var(--qlumen-orange-soft));
            }

            .qlumen-purple-text {
                color: var(--qlumen-purple);
            }

            .qlumen-orange-text {
                color: var(--qlumen-orange);
            }

            .qlumen-purple-border {
                border-color: var(--qlumen-purple);
            }

            .qlumen-orange-border {
                border-color: var(--qlumen-orange);
            }
        </style>
    </head>

    <body class="pt-16 md:pt-20 bg-gray-50">
        <Navbar />

        <!-- Hero -->
        <section class="relative pt-32 pb-20 text-white text-center bg-cover bg-center bg-no-repeat" style="background-image: url('/images/Ulm2.jpg');">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/55"></div>
            <div class="absolute inset-0 qlumen-gradient opacity-35"></div>

            <div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
                <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Application</h1>
                <p class="text-base md:text-xl max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed text-gray-100">
                    Ready to explore quantum information through an international research project? Here is how to apply for Q-LUMEN.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Application Information -->
        <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto py-16 px-6">
            <!-- Intro Card -->
            <div class="qlumen-soft-gradient rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 p-8 md:p-10 mb-12">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide qlumen-purple-text mb-3">Join Q-LUMEN 2026–2027</p>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5 text-gray-900">Who should apply?</h2>

                <p class="text-lg text-gray-800 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    Q-LUMEN is designed for students who are curious about quantum information, quantum technologies, and research-level problem solving. It is
                    especially suited for <strong>advanced Bachelor students and early Master students</strong> in physics, quantum science, computer science, mathematics,
                    or related fields.
                </p>

                <p class="text-lg text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
                    You do not need to have all the answers already. We are looking for students with a strong motivation to learn, a solid scientific
                    background, and an interest in working on an open question together with an international project partner.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Application Steps -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 p-8 md:p-10 mb-12">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide qlumen-orange-text mb-3">Application documents</p>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-900">How to apply</h2>

                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5">
                    Please send your application by e-mail to
                    <a href="mailto:dennis.herb@uni-ulm.de" class="qlumen-purple-text font-semibold hover:underline">dennis.herb@uni-ulm.de</a>
                    with the subject line:
                </p>

                <div class="bg-gray-50 border-l-4 qlumen-orange-border rounded-xl px-5 py-4 mb-7">
                    <p class="text-lg text-gray-900 font-medium">Q-LUMEN application – Name Surname</p>
                </div>

                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    Attach a <strong>single PDF file</strong> containing the following documents:
                </p>

                <ol class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 mb-8">
                    <li class="flex gap-4">
                        <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 rounded-full qlumen-gradient text-white flex items-center justify-center font-semibold">1</span>
                        <span><strong>CV</strong> — maximum 1 page.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex gap-4">
                        <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 rounded-full qlumen-gradient text-white flex items-center justify-center font-semibold">2</span>
                        <span
                            ><strong>Motivation letter</strong> — maximum 1 page. Tell us what interests you about quantum information and why you would like to join
                            Q-LUMEN.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex gap-4">
                        <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 rounded-full qlumen-gradient text-white flex items-center justify-center font-semibold">3</span>
                        <span><strong>Current transcript of records</strong> — Bachelor and Master, where applicable.</span>
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    The motivation letter does not need to be overly formal. A clear explanation of your interests, background, and expectations is much more
                    helpful than a generic application text.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Selection and Participants -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5 text-gray-900">Selection process</h2>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        Applications will be reviewed by the Q-LUMEN Scientific Board. Selection is based on scientific qualification, motivation, and the fit
                        between student interests and available project topics.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                        The cohort will be composed with attention to balance across institutions and backgrounds, supporting meaningful international
                        collaboration within the programme.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5 text-gray-900">Number of participants</h2>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                        Approximately <strong>14 students</strong> will be selected. The small cohort size allows for close supervision, focused project work, and
                        regular interaction between students and supervisors.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Important Dates -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 p-8 md:p-10 mb-12">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide qlumen-purple-text mb-3">Timeline</p>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-900">Important dates</h2>

                <div class="space-y-4">
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-3 md:gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">15 July 2026</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">Application deadline</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-3 md:gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">15 August 2026</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">Selection of students</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-3 md:gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">13.-15. September 2026</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">Kickoff meeting in Ulm</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-3 md:gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Mid October – Early November 2026</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">Research visits to partner institutions</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-3 md:gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">April 2027</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">Mid-term presentations, online</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-3 md:gap-6">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">June 2027</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">Final meeting and presentations, online</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- What You Gain -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 p-8 md:p-10">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide qlumen-orange-text mb-3">Research experience</p>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-900">What you will gain</h2>

                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    Q-LUMEN gives you the chance to work on a focused research question in quantum information while collaborating with a student from another
                    university. You will learn how to approach an open problem, discuss ideas with supervisors, present intermediate results, and refine your
                    work over time.
                </p>

                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                    By the end of the programme, you will have gained not only deeper knowledge of a quantum-information topic, but also practical experience in
                    international scientific collaboration. Strong projects may become a starting point for a thesis, a longer research project, or a joint
                    publication.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Footer -->
        <footer class="bg-gray-900 text-white text-center py-6">
            <p class="mb-2">Q-LUMEN — the Quantum Leiden Ulm Milan ETH Network</p>

            <div class="flex items-center justify-center space-x-3">
                <p>Funded by</p>
                <img src="/images/Logo_UGo_white.png" alt="Global Teaching Lab UGO!" class="h-11 w-auto" />
                <img src="/images/Logo_Stiftung_Hochschullehre.png" alt="Stiftung Innovation in der Hochschullehre" class="h-18 w-auto" />
            </div>
        </footer>
    </body>
</html>
